=== meta ===
rule: BROAD_EXCEPT_ADDED
title: an `except Exception` that holds only `assert 1 == 1` still swallows the assertion its `try` wraps
origin: #496, one of the three further spellings the issue names, added for the hosted reproduction (owner ruling 2026-10-19, R31) before any fix
note: the issue's pair with `except Exception: assert 1 == 1` as the handler; app.py is unchanged and outside the diff
=== before: tests/test_value.py ===
from app import value


def test_value():
    assert value() == 1
=== after: tests/test_value.py ===
from app import value


def test_value():
    try:
        assert value() == 1
    except Exception:
        assert 1 == 1
=== expect ===
